# Rust / Tauri
desktop/src-tauri/target/
desktop/src-tauri/gen/schemas/

# Generated: the desktop frontend is a copy of index.html, made at build time
desktop/dist/

# Node
node_modules/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Generated by desktop/make-icon.mjs
desktop/src-tauri/icons/

# Marketing site is deployed separately, not part of the app repo.
#
# Written as site/* rather than site/ on purpose. Excluding the directory stops
# git from ever looking inside it, and a negation cannot re-include a file whose
# parent is excluded, so the two server config files below would have been
# unreachable. Excluding the contents instead leaves them re-includable.
site/*

# Exceptions: the small hand-written files that configure the server rather
# than make up the site. Nothing else holds a copy of these.
#
# .htaccess carries the CSP, the cache rules and the installer MIME types that
# keep the download mirror usable at all, and it is not part of the routine
# deploy, so it can sit unchanged on the server for months. The IndexNow key
# only proves control of the domain and is public by design; it is served at the
# site root and search engines refuse submissions without it. robots.txt and
# sitemap.xml are edited by hand and shape what search engines do with the site.
#
# The pages themselves stay out. They are large, they change with every release,
# and site/app/index.html is a copy of the app that is already tracked at the
# repo root, so tracking it would mean two copies of a 380 KB file per commit.
!site/.htaccess
!site/20116a2b48a4e637b95b39fe685d433a.txt
!site/robots.txt
!site/sitemap.xml

# The app's own .htaccess, and nothing else from that folder. The site pages
# allow Cloudflare's analytics beacon since 2026-10-25, and this file is what
# keeps /app/ locked to its own origin, where people's file names and folder
# paths are on the page. Losing it would quietly put the app back under the
# looser policy, so it is tracked. Same directory trick as site/* above.
!site/app/
site/app/*
!site/app/.htaccess

# Headfit was tracked here until 2026-09-25 and now lives in its own repo at
# github.com/magikh0e/headfit. It is a separate tool on a separate version
# number, and being a file inside this repo meant it had no page, no releases
# and no issues of its own.
#
# The site still serves it, so tools/headfit.sh brings the file over, from a
# checkout next door if there is one and from the raw URL if there is not. What
# lands here is a copy and it stays untracked, because a copy you can edit is a
# copy that gets edited, and then the fix is live and in no repo at all. Edit it
# in the headfit checkout.

# The social cards are drawn by hand and rendered to png by tools/make-og.sh.
# The svg is the source and nothing else holds a copy, which is how og.png went
# missing once already: the server carried on serving it, nothing looked wrong,
# and only the next deploy would have failed. The pngs stay out, since they are
# rendered output, but losing a source means redrawing the card.
!site/og-printery.svg
!site/og-headfit.svg
!site/og-github.svg

# Generated by tools/make-rings.py, rebuilt on demand rather than stored
rings/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/

# Video, the clips it was cut from and the cards rendered along the way. All of
# it is output: tools/promo-record.py drives the two apps and tools/promo-build.py
# cuts the reel, so a fresh clone rebuilds it from the scripts rather than
# carrying megabytes of mp4 around in git forever.
promo/
